questions.explanation:
Three equivalent patterns:
```sql
-- LEFT JOIN + IS NULL (anti-join)
SELECT u.id FROM users u LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.user_id = u.id WHERE o.id IS NULL;

-- NOT EXISTS (usually best plan)
SELECT u.id FROM users u WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM orders o WHERE o.user_id = u.id);

-- NOT IN (careful with NULLs in orders.user_id)
SELECT id FROM users WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT user_id FROM orders WHERE user_id IS NOT NULL);
```
